WEBVTT

00:04:26.734 --> 00:04:30.249
The list of nuclear nightmares
tends to grow longer by the day.

00:04:30.273 --> 00:04:33.011
And there are a number
of former officials,

00:04:33.035 --> 00:04:34.774
as well as experts,

00:04:34.798 --> 00:04:38.051
who worry that right now,
we're in greater danger

00:04:38.075 --> 00:04:41.304
than we were in various points
in the Cold War.

00:04:42.759 --> 00:04:44.197
So this is scary.

00:04:44.877 --> 00:04:46.179
What can we do?

00:04:46.958 --> 00:04:48.108
Well, thankfully,

00:04:48.132 --> 00:04:49.298
["Duck and Cover"]

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:52.695
we don't have to rely
on the advice from the 1950s.

00:04:52.719 --> 00:04:53.727
(Laughter)

00:04:53.751 --> 00:04:55.736
We can take some control,

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:57.504
and the way we do that

00:04:57.528 --> 00:05:00.759
is by starting to ask
some fundamental questions